  "statuteText": "399-A:24 Consumer Credit Administration License Fund. –\n\nThe balance in the consumer credit administration license fund shall be transferred and shall be payable to the state treasurer as restricted revenue and credited to the appropriation for the commissioner, consumer credit administration division. Sums collected under this chapter shall be payable to the state treasurer as restricted revenue and credited to the appropriation for the commissioner, consumer credit administration division."
